    "paragraph": {
      "status": 200,
      "elapsed": 4.682,
      "text": "Rivers are among the most vital natural systems on our planet, carving valleys, nourishing soil, and sustaining countless ecosystems along their winding paths. From tiny mountain streams to mighty waterways like the Amazon or Nile, rivers connect landscapes and communities, providing water for drinking, agriculture, and industry. They support diverse wildlife, from fish to migratory birds, while also serving as vital transportation routes and sources of hydroelectric power. Beyond their practical uses, rivers hold cultural and spiritual significance worldwide, inspiring art, literature, and folklore. Protecting these dynamic, ever-flowing bodies of water remains essential for environmental balance and human prosperity alike.",
      "n_events": 7,
